{
  "index": 19,
  "response": " Here's a strategy to find the odd ball using three weighings:\n\n1. Weigh any two balls (A and B) against each other. If they balance, set them aside as likely normal weight balls. If one is heavier (or lighter), move on to step 2.\n\n2. Take the remaining ball(s) and weigh one of them against a known normal weight ball from step 1 (let's call it C). If they balance, the other unweighed ball(s) must be the odd ball. Weigh the odd ball against any other normal weight ball to confirm its abnormal weight (heavier or lighter).\n\n   If they don't balance in step 2:\n   - If the remaining ball is heavier (or lighter), it's the odd ball. Weigh it again against a known normal weight ball to determine if it's heavier or lighter.\n   - If the other unweighed ball(s) balance with each other, they are all likely normal weight balls, and the remaining ball is the odd ball. Weigh it against a normal weight ball to confirm its abnormal weight (heavier or lighter).\n\nBy following this strategy, you should be able to identify the odd ball and determine if it's heavier or lighter in just three weighings.",
